     The lliibbggppiioo library provides an interface to configure GPIO pins.  The
     library operates with a _g_p_i_o___h_a_n_d_l_e___t opaque type which can be created
     with ggppiioo__ooppeenn() or ggppiioo__ooppeenn__ddeevviiccee().  When no more GPIO operations are
     needed, this handle can be destroyed with ggppiioo__cclloossee().

     To get a list of all available pins, one can call ggppiioo__ppiinn__lliisstt().  This
     function takes a pointer to a _g_p_i_o___c_o_n_f_i_g___t which is dynamically allo‐
     cated.  This pointer should be freed with free(3) when it is no longer
     necessary.

     The function ggppiioo__ppiinn__ccoonnffiigg() retrieves the current configuration of a
     pin.  The pin number should be passed in via the _g___p_i_n variable which is
     part of the _g_p_i_o___c_o_n_f_i_g___t structure.

     The function ggppiioo__ppiinn__sseett__nnaammee() sets the name used to describe a pin.

     The function ggppiioo__ppiinn__sseett__ffllaaggss() configures a pin with the flags passed
     in by the _g_p_i_o___c_o_n_f_i_g___t structure.  The pin number should also be passed
     in through the _g___p_i_n variable.  All other structure members will be ig‐
     nored by this function.  The list of flags can be found in
     _/_u_s_r_/_i_n_c_l_u_d_e_/_s_y_s_/_g_p_i_o_._h.

     The get or set the state of a GPIO pin, the functions ggppiioo__ppiinn__ggeett() and
     ggppiioo__ppiinn__sseett() are available, respectively.  To toggle the state, use
     ggppiioo__ppiinn__ttooggggllee().

     The functions ggppiioo__ppiinn__llooww() and ggppiioo__ppiinn__hhiigghh() are wrappers around
     ggppiioo__ppiinn__sseett().

